  "implementation": [
    "Concrete HTTP administration and tenant readers retain the earlier actor/role exclusive deadline and their checked completion time in transient AgentAuthorityValidity.",
    "Setup API/query reads retain the bound after store and approver awaits; expiry or rollback returns content-free NotAuthorized before later reads or disclosure.",
    "Setup mutations, activation, provider mutation forwarding and interaction gate intents carry the same transient bound into final admission.",
    "EventStore dispatcher refuses expired authority before target construction and before submission, and rejects admission that drops or replaces the bound.",
    "Gateway-submitted outcomes remain authoritative after delayed acknowledgement; the local deadline does not rewrite accepted truth."
  ],
  "compatibility": {
    "publicContractsAndExistingConstructorSignaturesPreserved": true,
    "nullLifetime": "The optional lifetime grants no authority. Legacy default async administration providers still clear both role flags. Existing explicit host/test authorization adapters retain their port contract; concrete current-evidence readers always attach a bound on successful authorization. Existing machine/workflow intents without a human bound still require unchanged host admission.",
    "serializedState": "Lifetime objects are JsonIgnore and never added to logical payload, extensions, signatures, events, projections or public operation results.",
    "limits": "This is deadline/clock-order enforcement, not a new atomic revocation/effect protocol or proof of any production source, custody, signature, replay, denial spool or ACL."
  },
